{%- comment -%}
  robots.txt.liquid
  Version:      3.1.0
  Last updated: 2026-08-26
  Author:       Legendary Branding / Claude Code

  Changes from v3.0.0:
    — Removed /de, /fr, /es locale disallow rules from the wildcard group
      and all 7 named AI bot blocks. /de and /fr are live, published
      Shopify Markets locales — blocking them suppressed indexing of real
      storefronts, not "phantom" pages as previously assumed. /es is
      being opened ahead of upcoming LATAM sales via dlocal go.
    — Removed /*/collections/all-products disallow. Confirmed via live
      store data this is the "NEW DROPS" collection (126 products),
      linked from the homepage, empty-cart CTA, 404 page, and product
      recommendation blocks — not a low-value auto-generated page.
    — Removed /*/collections/vendors and /*/collections/types disallow
      rules. Confirmed neither collection exists on the store and
      neither path is referenced anywhere in the theme; the rules were
      inert dead weight.

  Changes from v2.0.0:
    — Added OAI-SearchBot (ChatGPT web search) and meta-externalagent (Meta AI)
      as named AI bot blocks for agentic commerce discovery.
    — Added Amazonbot named block for Amazon Alexa/shopping discovery.
    — Blocked Shopify collection sort URLs (/*?*sort_by=) to eliminate
      crawl-budget waste from sorted collection variants.
    — Blocked /search? — internal search result pages have low SEO value
      and create duplicate-content risk.
    — Blocked /*/collections/vendors and /*/collections/types — Shopify
      auto-generated taxonomy pages with no brand value.
    — Fixed utm pattern inconsistency: AI bot blocks now use /*?*utm_source=
      etc. (query-string-anchored) matching the wildcard group, replacing
      the imprecise /*utm_* path-level pattern.
    — Added no-slash locale variants (/de /fr /es) to all AI bot blocks,
      matching the wildcard group's handling.
    — Added explicit Sitemap directive to all named AI bot blocks so AI
      crawlers can locate the product catalog directly.

  Changes from v1.1.0 (see v2.0.0 header for full list).

  Agentic Commerce note:
    GPTBot (OpenAI training), OAI-SearchBot (ChatGPT web search/shopping),
    ClaudeBot, PerplexityBot, Google-Extended, meta-externalagent, and
    Amazonbot are explicitly allowed via named user-agent blocks.
    Explicit Allow signals cooperative intent and improves AI discovery
    ranking versus relying on inherited wildcard rules.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- comment -%} ─── SHOPIFY DEFAULT GROUPS ────────────────────────────────── {%- endcomment -%}
{%- for group in robots.default_groups -%}
  {{- group.user_agent -}}

  {%- for rule in group.rules -%}
    {{- rule -}}
  {%- endfor -%}

  {%- comment -%} Inject custom rules for the wildcard (*) user-agent only {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if group.user_agent.value == '*' -%}

